s in the United States, China, Canada, Poland, Mexico, France, South Korea, Russia, Japan, Germany, the United Kingdom, Spain, Italy, Czech Republic, Slovakia, Ukraine, Bulgaria, and internationally. The company was formerly known as Valeant Pharmaceuticals International, Inc. and changed its name to Bausch Health Companies Inc. in July 2018. Bausch Health Companies Inc. is headquartered in Laval, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas J. Appio | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20K people. Revenue per employee of $506K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $49K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Bausch Health Companies Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.1B market cap on $10.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 8.92\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.023354564755839153},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (43% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 95% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 65% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here's Why Bausch Health (BHC) is a Strong Momentum Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028692/here-s-why-bausch-health-bhc-is-a-strong-momentum-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3028692","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794491402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the BHC Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/39/Responsive_Playbooks_and_the_BHC_Inflection_111026031001_1794298201.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794298201.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bausch Health Cos (NYSE:BHC) Downgraded by Zacks Research to Hold","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/bausch-health-cos-nysebhc-downgraded-by-zacks-research-to-hold.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794074515.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"BHC Q3 Earnings Call Highlights Raised Outlook, Xifaxan Risks","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023043/bhc-q3-earnings-call-highlights-raised-outlook-xifaxan-risks?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog_plus%7Cearnings_call_takeaways-3023043","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793800800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company"